## What was ratified

Per OQ-1 resolution (requirements rev 2, 2e60b75) and design §2.4 (rev 2, 35818db):

- System seeding embeds are metered under `TENANT#__ISO_CANON__#METER` as **platform
  COGS** — never attributed to any real tenant.
- `systemOp: true` is threaded through the one-door embed path (`EmbedRequest` →
  `checkCreditBalance(tenantId, creditExempt)` SERVE-9 flag → `emitCreditsTelemetry`).
- `systemOp: true` on `telemetry.credits.consumed` is THE exclusion mechanism keeping
  platform-COGS seeding out of tenant invoicing — the billing signal stays clean per
  the owner's standing overage decision (2026-07-08: telemetry.credits.consumed is the
  billing signal; downstream overage consumer must be able to filter systemOp events).

## Context of ratification

The mechanism was flagged billing-adjacent at OQ-1 resolution and again in the
design-review and tasks-review reports; owner ratified 2026-07-17 (local) in direct
response to the architect's flag. Ratification arrived ahead of Phase 3 — the
dependency arrow Task 12 → Task 13 was scheduling (owner availability), not logic:
the task's content is confirmation of the MECHANISM, which is decision-complete.

Caveat on record: Task 12's live ACC-6 evidence (ISO_CANON meter row accumulates,
no real-tenant meter touched, telemetry events carry `systemOp: true`) remains an
open architect-lane closure. If the live evidence ever contradicts the ratified
mechanism, this ratification re-opens.

